Warning: no stdin data received in 3s, proceeding without it. If piping from a slow command, redirect stdin explicitly: < /dev/null to skip, or wait longer.
I fixed it in the shared helper, and `node test.js` now passes (prints `OK`).

**Root cause:** `pageCount` in `paginate.js:3` subtracted 1 whenever the item count was an exact multiple of the page size. With 6 invoices and a page size of 3 it returned 1 instead of 2. That one function caused both symptoms in the report:
- The printed page count was one too low.
- `pages()` uses `pageCount` to decide how many pages to build, so it stopped a page early and the last full page of invoices was dropped.

**Fix:** `pageCount` is now just `Math.ceil(n / size)`. `report.js` is unchanged, so anything else that uses `pageCount` or `pages` gets the fix too. `range.js` was already correct.

I also checked a few other counts with a page size of 3. Each one now gets the right number of pages, and every item comes back:

| Items | Pages |
|---|---|
| 0 | 0 |
| 1 | 1 |
| 3 | 1 |
| 4 | 2 |
| 9 | 3 |


